WEBVTT

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.380
The Tokyo Stock Exchange ended on an overall downward trend today...

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.550
He's on the move, Michael. How's it look on your end?

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.390
Okay. I've got him.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:17.800
Can you confirm?

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.000
The ID system gives me a positive.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.400
It's him, all right. He's right on schedule.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.230
Miss Karasuma, move to Point B.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:26.440
Roger.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:30.200
Haruto? Haruto, do you copy?

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.880
Hey, Michael, I'm having trouble reading you. What's wrong?

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.540
It's probably your channel. Make sure you're on the right one.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.850
I am, but...

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.220
Michael, do you read me?

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.390
Yeah, there's a bit of static...

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.150
Wait, he's here!

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:46.920
Commencing operation.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.730
Wait! He's changed directions!

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.700
He's turning the corner by the drugstore in block three.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.100
Haruto, did you catch that? He's acting suspicious.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:04.300
Haruto?

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:05.670
Hey, Haruto!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.680
Get clear! He's...

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.980
You can't go that way!

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.510
Disengage! We've been made!

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:27.160
What the...?!

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.200
What's wrong?

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.410
We don't have a surveillance system around there!

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:34.540
Do you read me?

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.480
Combat is too dangerous there!

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:35.680
Dammit...

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.310
Try to lead him onto a neighboring block!

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:49.890
Dammit...

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:02.000
The guy opened up on me... Was he a cop?

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.960
W-Who the hell are you?!

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.800
Bastard!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.440
The powers have no effect on me.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:24.360
W-Wait, are you people those "hunter" guys?

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.290
Quite possibly.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.580
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:04.310
...the instant I look away.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.450
I just kept counting...

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:14.890
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:22.260
...that I'd vomited up.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.200
In this time that seems so dry,

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:33.310
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:39.170
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.220
...and tears them to pieces.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:51.890
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:59.720
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.290
Ravens Flat...

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.640
Let's see, virgo...

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.980
Horoscope's pretty good. "A wonderful chance encounter may be close by."

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.570
Your lucky color is black.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.760
For crying out loud, you fired five bullets in the middle of the city!

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.620
Do you have any idea how long it took to retrieve them all?

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:20.890
Every time you go out there, you waste precious Orbo bullets.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.360
We're going to get another damages claim from the Factory!

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.470
Amon saves your hide every time you go out,

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:29.340
but if you don't get your act together soon...

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.880
Good morning, sir.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:38.170
I will have Sakaki submit an apology for last night's incident.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.280
I'll have him express his deepest apologies to the Factory.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.460
That's all right.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.030
Sir, about next year's budget estimates...

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.970
I believe you ought to handle the talks with the police department, Administrator.

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:00.340
Michael.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:02.310
Yeah?

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:03.840
Is everything ready?

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.670
Yes, Boss.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.150
In that case, let's get started.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:11.610
It looks like the witch that Amon hunted last night had a partner.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.420
The Factory's investigation turned this up.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:15.750
A partner? You mean a witch?

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.050
Of course.

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.450
It would seem that this "partner" has problematic powers.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.430
Hello?

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.230
A girl? By herself?

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.500
Well, Mr. Amon is...

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.310
Oh, he's in a meeting right now.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.610
Right, that's a good idea. Have her wait.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.280
I wonder what that was about...

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.650
Okay, here's that other witch's file.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.060
Name, Yuji Higashi. Age, 25. Unemployed.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.590
He met Kent Nishiyama, the witch we hunted last night, 10 months ago.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.860
They met down at the waterfront.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.730
And going back to what the Boss said a minute ago...

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:06.060
Nishiyama claims that he got his powers from Higashi.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.100
Of course, we know that's impossible.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:13.570
He probably just consciously realized that he himself had powers...

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:18.150
...after meeting someone else with similar abilities.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.850
So you're saying that he has the same powers as Nishiyama?

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.350
So it would seem.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:24.320
In any case, we'll track him down.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:28.020
There's a good chance that he also has information on us to some extent.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:31.030
We have to hunt him down before he goes to ground.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:34.920
This witch hunt takes priority over everything else right now.

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.470
That is all.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.160
Amon, come with me.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:50.280
A wonderful chance encounter... Lucky color is black...

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:03.820
Mornin'.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.400
"Morning"?

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:08.530
Miss Dojima, you just came in?!

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:10.530
Who's that?

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.710
Oh, she's here to see Mr. Amon.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:17.240
When you go up, could you tell him she's...

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.880
So, that's the kind of girl that Amon goes for...

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.440
What are you talking about?

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:26.190
Come on, if you don't hurry up, the Chief will get mad at you again.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.020
I know, I know. Stop rushing me!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.850
Dojima still isn't here.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:36.650
We can't do anything about it. She's special.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.330
I wish I was special, too...

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.200
Our team members' morale seems to be low lately.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:49.310
Do you suppose it's because we lost someone?

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:51.080
Most likely.

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:52.270
Well, no matter.

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:56.310
By the way, Solomon is sending us a replacement.

00:08:57.250 --> 00:09:00.180
A replacement? Six months after the fact?

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:05.580
They're up to something, don't you think?

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:11.060
We need a little more data to make an appeal to them regarding Orbo's effectiveness.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:13.730
Until then, I don't want headquarters to know.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.230
Be on your guard.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:18.060
Understood.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:21.770
It's me.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:24.500
Right.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:26.750
I see.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:34.470
The hunter they've dispatched is apparently a Craft User.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.250
A Craft User?

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.690
Dojima, the Chief's in a lousy mood.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.100
You never learn, do you?

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:47.470
Go do your best!

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:48.760
Dojima!

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:52.000
Do you have any idea what time it is?!

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.640
Hattori! The phone!

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.240
Oh, right! There's someone downstairs to see Mr. Amon, Chief.

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:01.480
Oh, that's Amon's girlfriend.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:02.340
What?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.310
I bet she's so obsessed with him that she followed him here.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.550
Poor kid.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:09.950
Huh?

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.160
Huh? We're in the middle of a crisis! This is hardly the time!

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.360
Amon has already left! Tell her so and get rid of her!

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.800
Dojima!

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.800
I hear we're getting a new hunter from headquarters.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.340
I guess the Administrator isn't happy with me.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:32.800
Who did you hear that from?

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:34.140
Who else?

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.180
Michael?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.280
Is that true, Amon?

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:41.280
Mr. Amon, if someone amazing shows up, am I gonna be fired?

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:42.820
Perhaps.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.450
Idiot, it's just a joke. Right?

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.190
A Craft User...

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:58.700
I'm really sorry about this. You'll be able to pass the time over there.

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:00.500
"Harry's," right?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:01.770
Yeah.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:02.930
I'll check it out.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:06.940
Be careful.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:11.470
Black, huh...

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:16.450
Dojima, how many times will I have to say this before it sinks in?

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:20.180
You saunter in and out whenever you feel like it.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.190
All I'm asking is that you treat this as a normal job.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:27.430
Keep this up, and you'll disappoint your father.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.070
It's me.

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:40.440
Oh.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.130
I see.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:45.640
She's gotten past immigrations, then?

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:48.610
I see. Get on her trail.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:50.920
Right.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.180
Any word, sir?

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:58.320
Apparently, she wasn't on the flight that headquarters said she'd be on.

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:03.230
Well, it wouldn't be the first time they gave us incorrect information.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:06.930
She might be making her way here on her own.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.490
Does she know where to find us?

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.100
If she didn't, she wouldn't be on the move by herself.

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:16.970
Here you are. One espresso.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:18.770
Thank you.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:24.940
Isn't that bitter?

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:29.450
No, it's traditional to drink this after a meal.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:31.750
So, you've been living overseas?

00:13:32.730 --> 00:13:36.250
I was born in Japan, apparently, but I don't remember it.

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.200
Oh, I see.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:41.430
I know it isn't much, but make yourself at home here.

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:42.960
Thank you.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.620
What do you two think you're doing?!

00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.800
The new hunter went missing at the airport!

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.590
At hectic times like this...

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:20.290
"Why do hunters cause nothing but trouble?"

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.300
Why do hunters cause nothing but trouble?

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:24.410
For crying out loud, only someone without a lick of sense...

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:27.040
...would wander off without waiting to be picked up!

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:32.320
The thought of getting another one of THOSE really makes me depressed.

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:33.850
Don't you think so, Hattori?

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.860
Yes, but I'm sure she felt she had a good reason.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:39.530
She's only fifteen! What reason could she possibly have?!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.260
Fifteen!

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:40.590
A girl...?

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:43.390
A girl who's barely out of her diapers is going to be hanging around here!

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:48.230
Yes, there was a girl here by herself.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.960
But the Chief told me to get rid of her, so I...

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:55.270
Yes, sir.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:59.140
She said she'd come by again this evening, so she left her luggage here with me.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:01.340
I see. All right.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:08.010
It would seem that the girl who was here to see Amon was our replacement hunter.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:13.120
I'm terribly sorry about the mix-up, sir. I'll have Dojima go look for her at once.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.530
Why me?!

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:15.590
This all started when...

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:17.360
No, we know where she is.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.300
I'll go pick her up.

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:22.270
Not at all, sir. I wouldn't dream of wasting your time, Administrator.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.760
I'll send Dojima.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.500
In the first place, all she does is loaf around the office with nothing to do.

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.540
Yes, you have a point. I'll have Dojima come with me.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:35.810
Yes, and?

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.250
The Boss and Dojima are tracking her down.

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:41.110
That's certainly an unusual combination.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:44.590
It must be because Dojima's actually seen the hunter's face.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:48.120
So, I hear she's fifteen? Why is she so...

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:49.560
Hang on.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:53.520
Okay, I found it!

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.770
This warehouse is what you were talking about, right, Amon?

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:58.200
I'm sending you the blueprints via nonlinear filter.

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:07.040
All I have is the layout. I couldn't find out what's going on inside right this minute.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:08.850
Well done.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:10.900
I sent it to Miss Karasuma and Haruto, too.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.290
So, what should I do now?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.250
Thank you for the meal.

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:20.390
I see... You dine Italian-style.

00:16:24.530 --> 00:16:26.620
Might I ask your name?

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.630
Robin. Robin Sena.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:32.400
Miss Robin, huh?

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:34.340
How long will you be staying here?

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:40.080
Well, that's not up to me. I'll be here for a while, though.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:41.240
I see...

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:43.650
Feel free to drop by again whenever you like.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:46.650
Thank you. I'll do that.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:01.130
Did that girl...

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:06.230
Gas pressure, maximum.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:09.540
All right!

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:18.610
Haruto and Miss Karasuma are on the move.

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:21.240
Their timing is right on schedule. How is it on your end?

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:32.860
I'm on schedule, as well. Now commencing operation.

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:44.340
Amon is in. How about you?

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:46.340
Now gaining entry.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.550
Be careful. Something's been bugging me for a while now.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:56.050
We've been making a lot of noise, but there's been no response from the witch.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:57.490
It's a little strange.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:59.120
Strange? Hey, now...

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:01.760
Ready?

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:02.120
Yeah.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:20.850
What's wrong?

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:23.410
I don't know! It looks like he's somewhere around the girders in back!

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.720
It's nothing. My feet got caught in some sand.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:31.190
Don't scare me like that, Haruto.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:32.620
Let's go.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:38.620
Idiots...

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:41.520
O tree of Yr, which proclaims true power...

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:43.430
Haruto?!

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.430
T-The Orbo isn't working!

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:50.940
A Craft?!

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:54.640
Yr!

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:26.140
An Ogham Wheel... The runes of Hagal's Eight...

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:28.250
But it's not right...

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:38.850
What's she...

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.620
Why don't we let her show us?

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:46.560
Let's see how a Craft User works in her native element.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:48.260
Yr!

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:03.610
What the...?

00:20:07.590 --> 00:20:08.550
What?!

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:12.420
A Craft User?

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:16.820
The replacement...

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:23.030
Your Ogham Wheel's ward was rewritten with Sig.

00:20:23.170 --> 00:20:25.030
This is my field.

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:44.590
You sons of...

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:07.440
Brain distortion value is below the red line.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.550
Michael, you can let in the guys from the Factory.

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.740
So, you're the replacement?

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:16.890
What are you doing?

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:21.620
Unlike headquarters, we capture witches alive.

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:23.260
Pretty humane, huh?

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:25.300
Capture?

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:29.220
Still, it looks like we got somebody amazing for a replacement.

00:21:29.900 --> 00:21:31.200
Right, Amon?

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:32.170
"Amon"?

00:21:33.570 --> 00:21:36.740
Do you think you could use that power of yours a bit more effectively?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.640
Putting out fires is a big hassle.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:44.580
Wait a minute, Amon!

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:48.290
Sorry, he's not exactly sociable.

00:21:56.660 --> 00:22:01.620
As expected, seeds of the Craft seem to have taken root in this country, as well.

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:04.530
What are you doing?

00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:06.000
Let's get going.

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:07.160
S-Sure.

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:22.050
Welcome to the STN-J.

00:22:36.660 --> 00:22:44.650
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.470 --> 00:22:47.510
Tell me.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:59.500
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:09.390
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:13.880
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:19.250
...all those promises...

00:23:21.190 --> 00:23:25.650
...inside me eventually...

00:23:24.940 --> 00:23:31.450
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:40.230
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
